Okay, here's a concise System Design Document for the "Hybrid Siddur" PWA based on what we've outlined:
System Design Document: Hybrid Siddur PWA (Conceptual Build)

1. Introduction
This document describes the system design for the "Hybrid Siddur," a Progressive Web App (PWA). Its primary goal is to offer a digital Jewish prayer book that dynamically renders prayer texts according to a user's selected personal Nusach (custom) and the Nusach of their community. The design emphasizes client-side operation and static hosting for simplicity and maintainability.

2. System Architecture
The Hybrid Siddur is a client-side PWA with no traditional backend server. All application logic and prayer data are bundled as static assets (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, JSON files). These assets are served by a static file host (e.g., GitHub Pages, Netlify) directly to the user's browser.
User's Browser (Web App Client): Executes all application logic, renders UI, and manages prayer display.
Static File Host: Stores and delivers index.html, style.css, script.js, sw.js (Service Worker), and JSON data files.

3. Core Components
Frontend (User Interface - UI):
HTML (index.html): Provides the basic structure with distinct views for the main menu, Nusach selection, and prayer display.
CSS (style.css): Styles the application and includes specific classes for visual differentiation of prayer texts based on Nusach (e.g., personal-only, community-only).
JavaScript (script.js): Contains all client-side logic, including UI interactions, data loading, Nusach selection handling, and the core prayer rendering engine.
Data Storage (Static JSON Files):
Prayer Templates (data/templates/*.json): Define the sequence and display rules for prayer units within each prayer (e.g., shacharit_template.json). Each unit has a unit_id and a display_rule.
Nusach Content (data/nusachim/*.json): Contain the actual Hebrew/Aramaic prayer texts for each supported Nusach (e.g., ashkenaz.json). Texts are keyed by unit_id.
Service Worker (sw.js): Enables PWA functionality, primarily caching static assets for offline access.

4. Data Model
Prayer Template JSON: An array of objects, where each object represents a prayer unit.
unit_id (String): Unique identifier, links to Nusach content.
section_name (String, Optional): Human-readable name.
display_rule (String): Defines rendering logic (e.g., "personal", "community", "hybrid_default_personal").
Nusach Content JSON: A JSON object where keys are unit_ids and values are the prayer texts for that specific Nusach.

5. Key Functionality
Dynamic View Management: JavaScript shows/hides HTML sections for different views (menu, Nusach selection, prayer).
Nusach Selection: Users select their "Personal Nusach" and "Community Nusach" from dropdowns populated from a predefined list in script.js.
Prayer Navigation: Users select a prayer (e.g., Shacharit, Mincha) from the main menu.
Dynamic Prayer Text Rendering Engine:
Fetches the selected prayer's template JSON.
Fetches the JSON content for the chosen personal and community Nusachim.
Iterates through the template units.
For each unit, applies the display_rule to determine which text (personal, community, or a combination/default) to display.
Applies CSS classes for visual cues (e.g., highlighting texts unique to one Nusach).
Offline Access: The Service Worker (sw.js) caches essential application files (index.html, style.css, script.js, core data JSONs) to allow the PWA to function without a network connection after the initial load.

6. User Flow (Simplified)
Launch: User opens the PWA URL. index.html and core assets load. Service Worker installs/activates.
Main Menu: User selects a prayer (e.g., "Shacharit").
Nusach Selection: User selects their personal and the community Nusach. Clicks "Start Prayer."
Prayer Display: The application loads the relevant template and Nusach data, then renders the prayer text according to the defined display_rules.
Navigation: User can return to the main menu.

7. Technology Stack
Frontend: HTML5, CSS3, Vanilla JavaScript (ES6+)
Data Format: JSON
PWA Features: Service Workers, Web App Manifest (manifest.json)
Deployment: Static web hosting.

8. Project File Structure (Key Files)
hybridsiddur-pwa/
├── index.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
├── sw.js
├── manifest.json
├── data/
│   ├── templates/
│   │   └── (e.g., shacharit_template.json)
│   └── nusachim/
│       └── (e.g., ashkenaz.json)
└── assets/
    └── icons/
        └── (app icons)




